; `set a[i]: v` on a CONTAINER is a hard diagnostic — report_subscript_assignment#.
;
; `operator []` answers the element BY VALUE (2026-08-27), so there is no slot
; behind `a[i]` and the emitter's Call target arm has no arm for a `[]` call:
; the statement was DROPPED, rc 0, with nothing said at the line that caused it.
;
; It cost four live miscompiles that stood for a day. tools/subscript.py's
; "74 buffer walks become subscripts" sweep rewrote four `set` TARGETS from
; `set *(x.get_buffer() + i): v` into `set x[i]: v`: dazzle's #!optional/#!key
; DEFAULTS were then never stored (every default read back as #f) and the
; root-rule specificity sort never swapped a pair. Five backend suites plus
; tests/dazzle/engine went red, and the engine red was written down as
; "not ours".
;
; The write is `put`; subscript_assignment_ok.scaly is the positive twin and
; pointer_subscript.scaly pins that a POINTER subscript still stores.
; xfail: cannot assign through a subscript

function main(argc: int, argv: pointer[pointer[const_char]]) returns int
{
    var a Array[int]()
    a.add(1)
    a.add(2)
    set a[1]: 42
    0
}
